I often have my healers drink from fountains more frequently
at early levels than other characters, just in case water demons
or water moccasins show up.  The sleep wand and the healing spells
really seem more useful than being able to fight like a Valk.

Conversely, my other classes often wimp out of drinking from
every fountain they see, until they Know they can handle four
angry water moccasins at once.

After all, it seems that the chances of getting blessed fountains
or tame demons, etc. is independent of your character level,
so you can often afford to wait until you can handle all the
bad side effects before you try for the good.

Roger Christman

Mini-spoiler alert:

I've often heard people shout that you should drink from every
fountain you see at least once, in case it's a magic fountain.
It seems that you can get up to six times the effect if your
luck is good (i.e. the effect up to six ways at once).


